  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Icod.Terminal 1.8.0 adds Kitty Graphics over APC as the second internal raster backend beneath the unchanged 1.7 TerminalRasterImage / DisplayRasterAsync semantic API. Direct raw RGB24/RGBA32 transfer uses deterministic bounded Base64 chunks; Indexed8 is adapted internally, including alpha-preserving RGBA expansion when required. A committed multi-frame Kitty transfer is serialized through the existing session-output boundary, honors caller cancellation before commitment, and is not automatically retried or switched to Sixel after partial output failure. Kitty capability is established by a correlated protocol query plus Primary DA barrier rather than terminal identity. Verified Kitty Graphics is preferred while verified Sixel remains fallback. APC response correlation, fragmentation, malformed/oversized input recovery, resource ceilings, lifecycle evidence invalidation, and subsequent-query integrity are hardened. Version 1.8 adds no public API and retains the 1.7 public API fingerprint. Full notes: https://github.com/uniblab/Icod.Terminal/blob/v1.8.0/docs/releases/1.8.0.md ; compatibility: https://github.com/uniblab/Icod.Terminal/blob/v1.8.0/docs/Compatibility-and-Versioning.md",
